    "body": "Local commit 45a020f on issue/150-coolant-followups (stacked on #147's issue/112-coolant), not pushed yet.\n\n- Coolant refusals in all six posts now start with `operation <name>:`.\n- A Flood op on a machine whose list holds only other kinds (for example Mist-only) is refused by name. An empty or unstated list, and a Flood entry with no code, still post without a coolant word (the unstated-limit law; see RECOMMENDED.md #150).\n- The machine editor offers Flood / Mist / Through-spindle / Through-tool plus a custom name. The posts also accept other spellings (\"Through spindle\").\n- New manifest flag `coolantModes = true`. When a script doesn't set it, the engine refuses any non-Flood op by name.\n- Tests added: coolant_followups.rs (7 tests) and the op page dropdown click test.\n\nGate: coolant, coolant_followups, conformance, posting, fanuc_post, lathe_post, machine, camcraft-post and the ui lib all pass. Clippy is clean on app, post and ui.\n",
